    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12447121/comment/12835233",
          "id": "12835233",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=h-aro",
            "name": "h-aro",
            "key": "h-aro",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Petr Nekvinda",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I suppose you use demo which comes with Lucene. Then try add \"JAVA_UNICODE_ESCAPE=true;\"  (without quotes) into options in HTMLParser.jj and regenrate lexical analyzer (javacc HTMLParser.jj). That solve problem for me.\n\n",
